COLUMNS
int ID
float GameCoords // the light's centre in yards, in the game's own frame (X north, Y west, Z up) -- the frame of the ADT terrain and of ZoneLightPoint: proven from the bytes (lights sit on the terrain under them far more often than chance; Classic Era's lights lie inside the zone polygons MoP Classic and Retail give the same Light ID); (0, 0, 0) is a map's default row
float GameFalloffStart // inner radius in yards: the light is whole inside it (the weighting is inferred, not proven); start <= end on 5354 of 5361 Retail rows and every Classic Beta row
float GameFalloffEnd // outer radius in yards: the light has no weight beyond it (inferred); 0 on most maps' default row
int ContinentID // the Map row the light belongs to: proven from the bytes (the same map on every Light ID Retail and Classic Beta share)
int LightParamsID // eight LightParams rows, one per condition; slot 0 is the clear-weather one (the slot meanings are the public definitions', not proven) and is set on every row but one (Retail Light 12616: 0): every non-zero value is a LightParams row, copy rows included (proven from the bytes)

COMMENT Written for WoW Model Viewer's light catalogue (wow::LightCatalog: the zone light's water colours,
COMMENT docs/world-viewer/09-liquids.md). The layout comes from public table definitions, read as hypotheses: every column
COMMENT the catalogue reads (database.xml, table Light) was checked against the clients' own bytes. Every field is listed in
COMMENT file order, so the positions are right for the layout below. Its hash is the same in Retail 12.1.5, PTR 12.1.7,
COMMENT Classic Beta 1.60.1, Classic Era 1.15.9 and MoP Classic 5.5.4. Classic Beta keeps 15 rows in two encrypted sections
COMMENT it has no key for; they read as zeros and are skipped. Classic Era has no zone polygons: it lights its zones with
COMMENT point lights of falloff ends up to 2,647 yd. A layout not listed here is not read.

LAYOUT 5F16BC84
BUILD 12.1.5.70448, 12.1.7.70424, 1.60.1.70450, 1.15.9.70003, 5.5.4.70268
COMMENT 5 fields in each client; IDs in the section's ID list (copy rows: Retail and PTR 12, Classic Beta and MoP Classic 1).
